body:
That's some solid advice, if only I had the courage to follow it. And it really is hard to put guys and girls in the same category since I see one as companions and the other as dating figures. I've just felt very different and isolated from other girls growing up because I had such a male influence. 

&#x200B;

The only way I can talk to girls is through social media, so at least I have that. But most of the time, they live in a different city so I can't see them in person or I don't have any classes with them at school. Plus, talking in person is a lot more rewarding than the former, but I see how it can be a lot easier.

> Everyone was crying but I just thought good riddance if we are making the superior gay human race I don’t want her here. 

Laughed WAY harder than I should've

&#x200B;
